<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Representation of the People Act 1918</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Representation of the People Act 1918 extended the vote to almost all men over 21 and, for the first time, to most women over 30 in the United Kingdom. Passed at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, it nearly tripled the electorate, and at the first election held under it, in December 1918, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> won most Irish seats.</p></div>
